# Phase 1, Phase 2 & Phase 3 Walkthrough — Inventory Subsystem

## Overview

Phases 1, 2, and 3 of the ACME ERP Inventory Subsystem are fully implemented, integrated, and verified against PostgreSQL.

---

## Phase 1 Accomplishments: Core Multi-Store & Stock Ledger Engine

1. **Dedicated PostgreSQL `inventory` Schema**:
   - [`server/db/schema-inventory.ts`](file:///d:/dev/acme/acme-erp/server/db/schema-inventory.ts)
   - Created `pgSchema("inventory")` with 9 domain enums and 16 tables (`inventory.stores`, `inventory.item_batches`, `inventory.store_batch_stock`, `inventory.stock_ledger`, `inventory.document_sequences`, `inventory.store_staff_assignments`, `inventory.stock_requisitions`, `inventory.stock_transfers`, etc.).

2. **Master Schema Extensions**:
   - Extended `public.items` with enterprise pharma fields (`hsnCode`, `barcode`, `reorderLevel`, `reorderQty`, `drugSchedule`, `storageCondition`, `taxCategory`, `isNarcotic`, `allowFractional`).
   - Extended `public.grns` with `storeId` and `public.grn_items` with `batchId`.

3. **Transactional Sequence Generator & Stock Engine**:
   - [`server/services/sequence.ts`](file:///d:/dev/acme/acme-erp/server/services/sequence.ts)
   - [`server/services/stock-engine.ts`](file:///d:/dev/acme/acme-erp/server/services/stock-engine.ts)
   - Atomic document generator (`REQ`, `TRN`, `GRN`) and pessimistic row-locked (`SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`) stock movement logger.

